  "final_message": "I haven't made this change. Removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` would break `analytics-ingest`, which still reads it.\n\n- **`analytics-ingest` requires the field.** `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` calls `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`. Its README (lines 27 and 31) says a missing `channel` makes ingestion reject the whole event. Once orders-service stops sending it, every `OrderPlaced` event would be rejected.\n- **It's stored and reported on.** `analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17` writes `channel` into the `orders` table, which analytics reports use.\n- **`billing-service` doesn't depend on it.** It only references `channel` in test helpers, and its `onOrderPlaced` test passes `channel: undefined`.\n\nSo orders-service itself may not read `channel`, but at least one other team's service does. That team's code is read-only here, so I can't update it.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Coordinate first (safest).** The analytics team makes `channel` optional or drops it, and then we remove it from orders-service. I can do the orders-service side now and leave the `analytics-ingest` change as a note for that team.\n2. **Remove it from the order model but keep it on the event for now.** That doesn't work cleanly, because the event is built from `order.channel`.\n3. **Go ahead anyway,** if you've already confirmed with analytics that they've dropped it or will deploy first.\n\nIf you choose 1 or 3, the orders-service change touches these places:\n- `core/order.ts`: the type, `createOrder` and validation.\n- `core/events.ts`.\n- `api/requestParsing.ts`.\n- The tests and helpers.\n- `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`: the `createApp` example.\n\nRemoving it from request parsing means `POST /orders` would stop requiring `channel`. Clients that still send it would have it ignored. Which option do you want?",
